---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HitaruJP | Privacy Policy"
  description="How the HitaruJP Japanese language app handles your personal data."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <h1 class="h2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: October 25, 2026.</p>

      <p class="body-copy">
        This Privacy Policy explains how the developer of HitaruJP ("the
        Developer", "we", "us", "our") collects, uses, stores, shares and protects
        your personal information when you use the HitaruJP Service. It should be
        read together with the Terms of Service, which govern your use of the
        app. We apply the data protection principles of Malawi's Data
        Protection Act and similar laws, and GDPR-style principles where they
        apply to users in the European Union or European Economic Area.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We collect the following personal information when you use HitaruJP:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Account information: your HitaruJP user ID, the email address you
          signed up with, and - when you sign in with Google - your Google
          account identifiers.
        </li>
        <li>
          Profile information: your display name, avatar, JLPT level, interests,
          and your subscription tier.
        </li>
        <li>
          Learning data: vocabulary, flashcards, review sessions, kana marks,
          saved sentences, activity days and visit counts, and watch history of
          catalogue videos.
        </li>
        <li>
          AI data: counts of AI explanations requested, tokens used and estimated
          cost.
        </li>
        <li>
          Device and technical information: device identifiers, operating system
          and version, app version, IP address, and diagnostics.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="body-copy">
        The backend API does not store email addresses; it stores the data listed
        above against your user record. We do not knowingly collect precise GPS
        location or payment information.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We use your information to create and authenticate your account, deliver
        the learning content and recommendations, run your flashcards and
        progress tracking, provide AI explanations, and understand how the Service
        is used so we can improve it.
      </p>

      <h2>Legal bases for our use</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We process personal data on the basis of consent (for example when you
        sign up and accept the Terms), the performance of a contract with you, our
        legitimate interests in operating and securing the Service, and legal
        obligations. We apply data protection principles - lawfulness and
        legitimacy of processing, purpose limitation, data minimisation, accuracy,
        storage limitation, integrity and confidentiality.
      </p>

      <h2>How we share information</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with the
        service providers that help us run the Service - including Google
        Firebase for authentication and storage, YouTube for videos and
        transcripts, and the AI provider for explanations - and with other users
        where your content is shared. We may also disclose information where
        required by law or to protect the rights and safety of people.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We keep your account information and learning data for as long as your
        account is active and needed to provide the Service. You can delete saved
        content and progress from within the app, and you may request deletion of
        your account and data by contacting the Developer. When you delete your
        account, we delete or deactivate the associated personal data, subject to
        any retention obligations under applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We use reasonable technical and organisational measures - including
        encryption in transit and access controls - to protect your information.
        No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot
        guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete,
        export or object to the processing of your personal data, and to withdraw
        consent. These rights may be provided directly by the data protection law
        that applies to you - including the GDPR for users in the European Union
        or European Economic Area, and Malawi's Data Protection Act. To
        exercise them, contact the Developer through the Serafim GitHub repository.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        HitaruJP is not directed at children below the minimum age described in
        the Terms of Service. We do not knowingly collect personal information
        from children. If we learn that we have collected it, we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Your information may be processed in Malawi and by service providers that
        may be located outside Malawi, including in other countries. Where data
        crosses borders, we rely on appropriate safeguards.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We may update this Privacy Policy. The current version is always available
        in the app and is marked with a date. Your continued use of the Service
        after a change takes effect means you accept the updated Policy. Questions
        about this Policy can be sent to the Developer through the Serafim GitHub
        repository.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Email:
        <a class="prose-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      </p>
      {
        site.phones.map((phone) => (
          <p class="body-copy">
            Phone:
            <a class="prose-link" href={`tel:${phone.replace(/[^+\d]/g, '')}`}>
              {phone}
            </a>
          </p>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  /* Quiet section heads: the h1 carries the page scale. */
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  .legal-meta {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
</style>
